The Stranger's storm, redrawn: mockup (waiting for .go before wiring)

Branch stills/stranger-storm-art, folder stranger-storm-art/ (images only):
  storm-phone-fire-turn.gif / .mp4 / .png     phone, light, a fire turn (fire leads)
  storm-phone-ice-turn.gif / .mp4 / .png      phone, light, an ice turn (ice leads)
  storm-computer-fire-turn.gif / .mp4 / .png  computer, dark, a fire turn
  storm-computer-ice-turn.gif / .mp4 / .png   computer, dark, an ice turn
  before-phone-todays-ring.png                today's pixel ring, the same moment, for comparison
The GIFs are 256 colors at 15 frames a second; the MP4s show the true colors (same frames). The PNGs are full screens.

What it is
- Real screenshots of a Stranger battle (?power=storm), today's ring hidden, the new storm composited the way the game will do it:
  the loop's frames on one small canvas (400 px, scaled up), neighbors cross-faded, the still frost under it.
- Fire up the left and across the top-left (yellow-white cores, orange, deep red edges, embers); frost wind, crystal shards, snow and
  icicles down the right and along the bottom-right; both turn the same way round and meet at the top's and the bottom's middle.
- A 3 s seamless loop, 30 frames. On a fire turn the fire is full and doubled (a second copy half a loop on), the ice at 80%; on an
  ice turn the other way round.
- Over the board the storm is see-through and reaches about a third of an edge square; its bright part sits on the frame and margin.
  Along the bottom it barely reaches past the board, so the line under it (what to do, the clock) stays readable.

What ships (measured from these frames, after compression; the mockup is cut back out of these files)
- storm.webp: 3264 x 2000, 1029 KB (30 frames, a fire cell and an ice cell each, 272 x 400). frost.webp: 544 x 800, 34 KB (still).
  About 1.06 MB in all, loaded when a Stranger battle starts. About 26 MB once decoded (the price of 30 frames at this size).
- At play time: 2 to 6 image draws a frame on one 400 px canvas (no particles), plus one still image under it.
- Drawn offline by scripts/storm-art/render.py (numpy + Pillow, about 40 s), packed by pack.py; preview.py made these mockups.

Calls for the director / Eric
1. On a computer the top of the storm crosses the thin boss strip above the board (his name, the move count). Today's ring does
   too. Say if the top should be held back like the bottom.
2. On a phone the board nearly fills the width (14 px each side), so the side flames show mostly over the a- and h-file's outer third.
3. The crack of the opening scene (lava-orange / ice-blue) is not in this mockup: I'd recolor the existing SVG cracks by side when
   wiring (cheap), not draw new art. Say if you want more.
4. Decoded size: 24 frames instead of 30 (a 2.4 s loop) or 360 px frames would cut it by about a fifth each, if 26 MB is too much.
